  "reviewAxes": {
    "correctness": "Read all nine complete owned sources, proposal, proof/route/current-backup dependencies and final repairs. Complete exact assets and same-key live-manifest locator, channel/expiry/storage-schema/rollback floor and opaque candidate are enforced; corrupt/foreign state refuses without reset. Atomic floor precedes explicit destination navigation and remains after failure.",
    "security": "Default null trust touches no other ports. Actual G05 exact URL capture, credential/referrer omission, redirect/body/deadline/generation constraints and physical drain are retained. Native T34/profile-lock generation and actual physical EIP1193 promise lease block transition while pending, including after abort. Both independently reproduced callback-boundary findings are closed.",
    "architecture": "Internal opt-in controller and narrow untrusted parser wrappers remain outside default facade/App. Type-only HttpFetchPort export does not issue authority. No bootstrap, key rotation, archive, nonempty deployment, production source/route/wallet profile or secret transfer is adopted.",
    "readability": "README accurately separates configured capabilities, signed facts, local fixtures, physical admission and missing production profiles. Fixed identity-classified errors avoid probing hostile exceptions.",
    "performance": "Count/byte limits, per-G05 operation30s and aggregate120s are explicit; cleanup/drain remains owned through ignored native work, and assets/count bounds do not claim heap/CPU/mobile feasibility."
  },
